Google App Engine – Deploy a Flask App

Part 1 — Install Google Cloud CLI

Step 1: Install Google Cloud CLI

Install Google Cloud CLI on your computer.

After installation, open Command Prompt / PowerShell and check:

gcloud --version

Step 2: Login

gcloud auth login

A browser will open → sign in with your Google account.


---

Part 2 — Create the Flask Application

Step 3: Create a project folder

mkdir my-app
cd my-app

Step 4: Create main.py

Create a file named:

main.py

Put this code inside:

from flask import Flask

app = Flask(__name__)

@app.route("/")
def hello():
    return "Hello from Google App Engine!"

if __name__ == "__main__":
    app.run(host="0.0.0.0", port=8080)


---

Step 5: Create requirements.txt

Create:

requirements.txt

Put:

Flask


---

Part 3 — Create Virtual Environment

Step 6: Create virtual environment

On Windows:

python -m venv venv

Step 7: Activate it

venv\Scripts\activate

You should see something like:

(venv) C:\...\my-app>

Step 8: Install Flask

pip install Flask

Or install everything from requirements:

pip install -r requirements.txt


---

Part 4 — Test the Application Locally

Step 9: Run the Flask application

python main.py

You should see something similar to:

Running on http://127.0.0.1:8080

Open your browser and go to:

http://127.0.0.1:8080

You should see:

Hello from Google App Engine!


---

Part 5 — Create Google App Engine Configuration

Step 10: Create app.yaml

Inside the same folder, create:

app.yaml

Put:

runtime: python312

So your folder should look like:

my-app/
│
├── main.py
├── requirements.txt
├── app.yaml
└── venv/


---

Part 6 — Configure Google Cloud

Step 11: Login

If you haven't already:

gcloud auth login

Step 12: Initialize Google Cloud

gcloud init

Choose your Google account and then select an existing Google Cloud project or create a new one.

You can check the currently selected project with:

gcloud config get-value project


---

Part 7 — Create App Engine Application

If App Engine has not been initialized for your project, run:

gcloud app create

It will ask you to select a region.

Choose the region required for your lab/project.

> Important: The App Engine region generally can't be changed later for that project.




---

Part 8 — Deploy the Application 🚀

Make sure you are inside the folder containing app.yaml:

cd my-app

Then:

gcloud app deploy

It will ask you to confirm.

Enter:

Y

Google Cloud will upload and deploy your Flask application.


---

Part 9 — Open the Deployed Application

After deployment:

gcloud app browse

This opens your deployed application in the browser.

You can also use:

gcloud app browse --project=YOUR_PROJECT_ID


